  {
   "n": 28,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +2 / -0",
   "html": "<p>Which of the following is/are correct?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "In a min-heap, the next largest element of any element can be found is Ο(log <em>n</em>) time."
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "In a BST, finding the next smaller element to given element can be done in Ο(<em>n</em>) time."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "Binary heap to BST conversion take Ο(<em>n</em> log <em>n</em>) time."
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "BST to binary heap conversion take Ο(<em>n</em>) time."
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "B",
    "C",
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B, C, D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>(b, c, d)<br />\n(a) False: A min-heap can provide next largest element, we need to do a linear search through the<br />\nheap&rsquo;s array, it will take &Omicron;(n) time.<br />\n(b) True: Find the next smallest element, the predecessor, may require travelling down the height<br />\nof the tree, making the running time &Omicron;(n) in worst case.<br />\n(c) True: Binary heap to BST conversion take &Omicron;(n log n) time.<br />\n(d) True: By heapify method.</p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 29,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE & IT • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>Consider we constructed binary search tree shown below starting with an empty tree and elements 2, 7, 12, 14, 15, 20, 25, 28, 30 and 40 are come in any order:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/99dfc664297c3731642d.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which of the following about the order of elements in input sequence can be true?</div>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "12 comes before 7 and 2 comes after 7"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "28 comes after 25 and 20 comes after 7"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "20 comes before 7 and 12 comes after 7"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "25 comes before 28 and 14 comes after 15"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C",
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "C, A, B, D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>(c)<br />\nWe know that &lsquo;a&rsquo; comes before &lsquo;b&rsquo; iff &lsquo;b&rsquo; is child of &lsquo;a&rsquo; and &lsquo;b&rsquo; comes after &lsquo;a&rsquo; iff &lsquo;b&rsquo; is child of &lsquo;a&rsquo;.<br />\nOption (a) 7 is not the child of 12. So false<br />\nOption (b) 20 is not child of 7. So false<br />\nOption (d) 14 is not child of 15. So false<br />\nOnly option (c) is correct i.e. &lsquo;7&rsquo; is child of &lsquo;20&rsquo; and &lsquo;12&rsquo; is child of &lsquo;7&rsquo;.</p>"
  },
